  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 14-layer planar multilayer stack with sequence: air incident, then hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), on Al (Rakic-LD) substrate. All 14 layer thicknesses are tunable variables. Initialize Cr (Rakic-LD) layer (index 2) thickness with uniform random draws in 5-30 nm range. Initialize all dielectric layers near quarter-wave estimates (50-300 nm range). Apply 2x step-size multiplier or increased mutation variance to Cr (Rakic-LD) layer during first 5 optimization iterations. Illumination: normal incidence, unpolarized, wavelength range 400-2000 nm. Objectives: maximize mean absorptance in 400-700 nm band, maximize mean reflectance in 700-2000 nm band. Total layer count fixed at 14. Use coherent transfer matrix method solver.",
